509	# Real-app demo recording
510	
511	Records the 2-minute Mimi demo from the **real app** (`/app/?live=1`), not the mock in `../mock/`. One command,
512	one uncut take, with the sound the app actually played.
513	
514	| Beat | What runs | Live or simulated |
515	|---|---|---|
516	| Owner says "my cat Mimi is limping" | Gemini Live hears the line through a virtual microphone and answers out loud | Live (the owner's line is a pre-generated Gemini TTS clip, `owner-line.wav`) |
517	| Triage card | Gemini Live calls the care tool, the backend runs Gemini care triage | Live |
518	| Nearby clinics | Backend clinic search around Zurich | Live (Gemini Maps grounding, needs `GEMINI_API_KEY`) |
519	| German vet script | Gemini drafts the German script with English subtitles | Live |
520	| Vet and insurer calls | The app's phone rehearsal: Pawse's German lines spoken by Gradium | Gradium voice live, the vet's and insurer's replies simulated and labelled so on screen. Nothing is dialled |
521	| Summary | Plan page built from the steps above | Live UI over the simulated call results |
522	
523	The stage around the phone shows a caption per beat and `LIVE` / `SIMULATED` badges, so nothing simulated is
524	presented as real.
525	
526	## Run
527	
528	Needs Linux with Xvfb, PulseAudio (`sudo apt-get install pulseaudio pulseaudio-utils xvfb`), ffmpeg, Node 20+,
529	`npm install` in `demo/`, the app built (`cd web && npm run build`) and the backend running with `GEMINI_API_KEY`
530	and `GRADIUM_API_KEY` in `.env`:
531	
532	```sh
533	uvicorn pawse.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765 &
534	bash demo/real/record-real.sh          # APP_URL=... to point at another server
535	```
536	
537	Output in `/mnt/pawse-demo-out/` (`OUT_DIR=` to change): `pawse-demo-real.mp4` (deliverable, silent waits shortened to fit 2:00 by `make-cut.py`; speech is never cut), the raw `.mkv`, and `-marks.json` (when each
538	caption appeared). A failed beat stops the take and saves `-fail.png`.
539	
540	To change the owner's spoken line: `python demo/real/make-owner-line.py "<text>" demo/real/owner-line.wav`
541	(Gemini TTS, reads `GEMINI_API_KEY` from `.env`).
542	
543	The opening has a narrator (`narrator-intro.wav`, Gemini TTS voice Charon, about 12 s) played into `rec` only, so
544	Gemini Live never hears it; the clip's own sound drops under it and the app starts only after it ends. Skip it with
545	`NARRATION_WAV= bash demo/real/record-real.sh`. To change it: `python demo/real/make-owner-line.py "<text>"
546	demo/real/narrator-intro.wav Charon` (write Pawse as "Pause" so TTS says it right).
547	
548	## How the sound gets in
549	
550	PulseAudio gets two null sinks. Chromium plays into `rec`, and ffmpeg records `rec.monitor` together with the X
551	screen, so picture and sound share one clock. The owner's line is played into `mic`, which Chromium sees as the
552	microphone `owner_mic`, and also into `rec` so viewers hear it. Every take differs a little: Gemini's wording and
553	timing are live.
